From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 03:57:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: skip a monitor without a source in
 DisplayConfigGetDeviceInfo

NtUserDisplayConfigGetDeviceInfo (sysparams_ios.c, the iOS build's copy of
Wine's sysparams.c) looks a target up by its output id and
then compares the adapter LUID through monitor->source->gpu. A monitor
can have no source (a detached one; the rest of sysparams.c checks for
it), and its output id can match the one asked for, so the lookup read
through a NULL source while holding display_lock.

World of Warcraft's ARM64 client asks for
DISPLAYCONFIG_DEVICE_INFO_GET_ADVANCED_COLOR_INFO before it creates its
D3D12 device. On the phone the read faulted (address 0x120,
source->gpu), the access violation went to the game's handler, which
went on, and display_lock stayed locked: the main thread's next
vkGetPhysicalDeviceProperties (get_gpu_info_from_uuid) waited on it
forever, before any window or frame.

A monitor without a source belongs to no adapter, so the target-name,
preferred-mode and advanced-color lookups now pass over it, as
NtUserQueryDisplayConfig does.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-31-wow-arm64-start.md
Offered-upstream: not yet; WineHQ 11.20's sysparams.c has the same lookups
---
 build/win32u-unix/sysparams_ios.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/win32u-unix/sysparams_ios.c b/build/win32u-unix/sysparams_ios.c
index 1916700..94a4c39 100644
--- a/build/win32u-unix/sysparams_ios.c
+++ b/build/win32u-unix/sysparams_ios.c
@@ -8513,7 +8513,7 @@ static NTSTATUS display_config_get_device_info_unlogged( DISPLAYCONFIG_DEVICE_IN
 
         LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY(monitor, &monitors, struct monitor, entry)
         {
-            if (target_name->header.id != monitor->output_id) continue;
+            if (!monitor->source || target_name->header.id != monitor->output_id) continue;
             if (memcmp( &target_name->header.adapterId, &monitor->source->gpu->luid,
                         sizeof(monitor->source->gpu->luid) ))
                 continue;
@@ -8560,7 +8560,7 @@ static NTSTATUS display_config_get_device_info_unlogged( DISPLAYCONFIG_DEVICE_IN
 
         LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY(monitor, &monitors, struct monitor, entry)
         {
-            if (preferred_mode->header.id != monitor->output_id) continue;
+            if (!monitor->source || preferred_mode->header.id != monitor->output_id) continue;
             if (memcmp( &preferred_mode->header.adapterId, &monitor->source->gpu->luid,
                         sizeof(monitor->source->gpu->luid) ))
                 continue;
@@ -8665,7 +8665,7 @@ static NTSTATUS display_config_get_device_info_unlogged( DISPLAYCONFIG_DEVICE_IN
 
         LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY(monitor, &monitors, struct monitor, entry)
         {
-            if (color_info->header.id != monitor->output_id) continue;
+            if (!monitor->source || color_info->header.id != monitor->output_id) continue;
             if (memcmp( &color_info->header.adapterId, &monitor->source->gpu->luid,
                         sizeof(monitor->source->gpu->luid) ))
                 continue;
